q-95217" :question/id #uuid "2ffbd9a8-0125-537f-b30a-fb56bc0ed6f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95217" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{10\\times 2}(R),$ the vector space of all $10\\times 2$ matrices over $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R)$ contains a total of $n\\cdot m$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 2}(R)$ contains $3\\cdot 2=6$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{10\\times 2}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{10\\times 2}(R))=10\\cdot 2=20.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95217/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b61a755f-23e8-5039-b2f5-b5984fdb420c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95226/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "2f68bd85-aad1-54fc-b806-3c6a7f5142b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95226/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6bc8e09b-ec5c-520f-b979-385547908338" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95226/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9f92a4