\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{15}[t])=15+1=16\\ne 15.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{15})=15.\\,✓\n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-95226/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95226"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106900/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ef224d18-d2d8-50f0-8882-6d9de91b4dba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106900/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0ad599c0-862b-50a6-b9df-bfcf149636c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106900/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "8cc58ad8-ba34-5853-a9ea-ca8443ddb766" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106900/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c9168d96-4a75-5552-85e9-b479abc7fe39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106900/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "431a3acb-ddbf-5414-82b1-d9179fae9f6f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106900/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb23244-e225-52e7-8c8a-cc565155a106" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106900/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-106900/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-106900/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-106900/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-106900/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-106900/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106900" :question/id #uuid "08bf3d03-6691-5a28-9f42-839a1c9ba54b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106900" :question/problem "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $3?$\n\n- ${R}^{2}$\n- ${R}_{2}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{3}(R),$ the vector space of all $3\\times 3$ matrices over $R$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{2})=2\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{2}[t])=2+1=3.\\,✓\n$$\n- Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{3}(R))={3}^{2}=9\\ne 3.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106900/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aee17e3a-031d-5c0e-9488-17410b3a2372"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106900"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106897/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "bfd1d889-3694-593d-9c62-40c3c502580c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106897/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "99169741-725